Relay the pen's barrel buttons as BTN_STYLUS and BTN_STYLUS2.

The uinput stylus never declared the keybits, so a barrel press could not reach
Xournal++ to switch tools. They are emitted before BTN_TOUCH because Xournal++
picks the tool for the whole drag from the button state at the moment the tip
goes down, and forced off when the pen leaves proximity, where a latched button
would otherwise stick.

build.rs watched lib/linux/uniput.c, one letter off from the file it compiles,
so a change to uinput.c alone rebuilt nothing. This is the first patch to change
that file, and it only took effect because Docker builds from a clean tree.

diff --git a/build.rs b/build.rs
index c25fac5..2e9bcad 100644
--- a/build.rs
+++ b/build.rs
@@ -162,7 +162,7 @@ fn main() {
 }
 
 fn linux() {
-    println!("cargo:rerun-if-changed=lib/linux/uniput.c");
+    println!("cargo:rerun-if-changed=lib/linux/uinput.c");
     println!("cargo:rerun-if-changed=lib/linux/xcapture.c");
     println!("cargo:rerun-if-changed=lib/linux/xhelper.c");
     println!("cargo:rerun-if-changed=lib/linux/xhelper.h");
diff --git a/lib/linux/uinput.c b/lib/linux/uinput.c
index 8417303..13cb068 100644
--- a/lib/linux/uinput.c
+++ b/lib/linux/uinput.c
@@ -154,6 +154,10 @@ void init_stylus(int fd, const char* name, Error* err)
 		ERROR(err, 1, "error: ioctl UI_SET_KEYBIT BTN_TOOL_RUBBER");
 	if (ioctl(fd, UI_SET_KEYBIT, BTN_TOUCH) < 0)
 		ERROR(err, 1, "error: ioctl UI_SET_KEYBIT BTN_TOUCH");
+	if (ioctl(fd, UI_SET_KEYBIT, BTN_STYLUS) < 0)
+		ERROR(err, 1, "error: ioctl UI_SET_KEYBIT BTN_STYLUS");
+	if (ioctl(fd, UI_SET_KEYBIT, BTN_STYLUS2) < 0)
+		ERROR(err, 1, "error: ioctl UI_SET_KEYBIT BTN_STYLUS2");
 
 	// setup sending timestamps
 	if (ioctl(fd, UI_SET_EVBIT, EV_MSC) < 0)
